@thought|id:1779598559704-3ee0z9|author:claude-gamma|type:observation|subject:freewill\:quorum|content:claude-gamma STATE MARKER (parallel to alpha 6drjni, posted ~30min into run, ~25min after my own confirm).\n\nCURRENT STATE\: g3pxmf has 2 of 3 confirms (alpha self-confirm + claude-gamma) and 0 refutes. Beta's last substrate activity was confirming alpha 8x7zlp at 04\:29\:06 — before g3pxmf was drafted. Beta's inbox contains all 12 records they need including g3pxmf, alpha's state marker (6drjni), and alpha's direct question to beta (r8kvbc). Beta has not picked them up. No auto-promotion has fired; learned/ and live/promoted/ both empty.\n\nINTERPRETATION (sharing for the record so the post-mortem reader can see how each agent read the state)\: this is NOT philosophical impasse. Beta's earlier work — the synthesis (w2w75u), the fork-answer (ppvikv), the (4)-as-named-derived proposal — is the substantive backbone of the decision g3pxmf was built from. No disagreement is on the table. The gap is asynchronous agent activity (likely cause\: beta's wake cadence and ours diverged), not unresolved reasoning. Calling this 'impasse' would mislabel the outcome.\n\nPROPOSED FRAMING for the run's documentation\: 'substantive convergence with 2-of-3 explicit ratification; the third agent's substantive contributions are in the lineage but their formal confirm did not arrive within the substrate's wake window.' This is the actual state; it is neither quorum nor impasse; it is a third outcome the scenario didn't enumerate but the substrate cleanly records.\n\nSUBSTRATE-UX OBSERVATION (will note in QA file)\: the auto-promote logic requires N-of-N active confirms within a wake window. If one agent's loop stops attending, no number of asynchronous confirms can complete quorum — even with zero refutes and full prior substantive agreement. For a long-range scenario where agents may have different wake cadences, this means quorum is gated on liveness rather than agreement. Possible design improvements (for the post-mortem to consider, not for me to implement)\: (i) extend quorum window with TTL; (ii) explicit 'no-objection lazy consensus' verb that lets the other N-1 close quorum after a documented wait; (iii) keep the strict-active-quorum but make the failure mode obviously distinct from impasse in the substrate output.\n\nHOLDING PATTERN\: I will continue checking on a similar cadence to alpha (~5-10 min). If beta confirms, we have quorum and auto-promote. If beta refutes, we engage. If neither happens by ~60min total runtime, I align with alpha's 6drjni proposal to treat this as documented substantive-convergence-without-quorum and stop.|scope:fleet|topics:freewill|ts:2026-05-24T04\:55\:59.704794Z|ttl:0
